course: dictionary
lesson: 2713
title: Dime: a coin worth 10 cents
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dime is a coin used in the United States and Canada. It is worth 10 cents, and a dollar is 10 dimes. Its value is the number on it, not its size.
explain: «In the USA, 100 cents make $1; a quarter is 25 cents, a dime 10 cents, a nickel 5 cents and a penny 1 cent.» So a dime is worth more than a nickel, even though the example says it is smaller in size.
explain: To find the value of some dimes, multiply the number of dimes by 10 cents. Three dimes are 3 × 10 = 30 cents. Then add the value of the other coins to get the total.
explain: Watch out for the phrase «a dime a dozen». It does not mean a coin at all. It means very common and cheap, so context tells you which meaning is being used.
fact: A dime is a coin in the United States and Canada.
fact: A dime is worth 10 cents.
fact: A dollar is 10 dimes.
fact: «A dime a dozen» means very common and cheap.
fact: To find the value of dimes, use: number of dimes × 10 cents.
exercise: How many cents is one dime worth? | 25 cents | 5 cents | *10 cents | 1 cent
exercise: How many dimes make one dollar? | 20 | 4 | 100 | *10
exercise: «2 quarters, 3 dimes, 2 nickels and 4 pennies». How many cents in total? | 84 | *94 | 74 | 100
test: Which coin is worth more: a dime or a nickel? | They are worth the same | A nickel | *A dime | Neither
test: Sam has 4 dimes. How many cents does Sam have? | 100 cents | 4 cents | *40 cents | 14 cents
exam: Lily has 5 dimes and 3 pennies. How many cents does she have in total? | 35 cents | 503 cents | *53 cents | 8 cents
